2026-09-27T09:27:24.4261922Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4262165Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4262614Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4262884Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4262974Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4263180Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4263292Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4263456Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4263808Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4264009Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4264121Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4264379Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4265020Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4265159Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4265562Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4265919Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4266562Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4267073Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4267177Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4267587Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4268099Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4268371Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4268655Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4334128Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4334256Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4334743Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4334878Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4336317Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4337745Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4337995Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4338469Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4339301Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4339889Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4340468Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4340893Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4341290Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4341410Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4341650Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4341790Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4342838Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4343972Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4344847Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4345720Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:24.4345937Z 
